# <area>: <what changed, imperative, <=72 chars>
# |<---- keep the subject inside this line, 72 chars ---------------->|
#
# Areas used here: sgurr_cpp, nnue, testing, benchmarks, web, docs, ci,
# chore, release, nets, tools.
#
# Then a blank line, then the body. The body is where this project's
# commits earn their keep, so it is worth writing:
#
#   - WHY, not what. The diff already says what changed.
#   - The measurement, with its error bar and game count, if one exists.
#     "+21.2 +/-8.7 over 4,000 games" not "improves strength".
#   - The bench fingerprint if the change was meant to be speed-only, or a
#     note that it moved if it was not.
#   - What was ruled out, and how. A negative result recorded here is worth
#     more later than a confident sentence with nothing behind it.
#
# Wrap the body at 72 characters.
#
# Install this template with:
#     git config commit.template .gitmessage
